# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cli-options-host-default-is-deprecated-mock — the --host default is stored as the deprecated alias :mock
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-cli-options-host-default
#+DATE: 2026-11-13

* Context

Found while answering "what is the default of --host?" (see
=cli-option-environment-defaults=). The documented default is =cador=
(=clautolisp --help=: "cador (default)"; =*host-descriptions*=).

* Problem

The shared =cli-options= struct initialises the slot to the deprecated alias:

: (host :mock)   ; AC  :mock / :null (default :mock)
  — =clautolisp/autolisp-cli/source/options.lisp=

- clautolisp copes: its HAL-backend constructor maps NIL and =:mock= to cador.
- alfe does not know =:mock=: =+alfe-hosts+= is =cador= / =cadtui= / =nihil=
  only, and =%parse-alfe-host= rejects =mock=. Yet with no =--host=, alfe
  carries =:mock= through — =alfe --dry-run= prints =host: MOCK=, and the
  =--debug= trace logs =host :MOCK= — a value alfe would refuse on its own
  command line.
- The slot comment is stale (=:mock= / =:null=; the hosts are now
  cador/cadtui/nihil).
- Related: clautolisp's =parse-host= yields =:nihil= for =nihil= but =:null=
  for the aliases =null= / =none=, two keywords for one host; check every
  consumer treats them alike, or fold the aliases onto =:nihil=.

* Proposal

Default the slot to =:cador=, update its comment, and fold the =null= /
=none= aliases onto =:nihil= (or prove both keywords are handled
everywhere).

* Acceptance criteria

- =alfe --dry-run= with no =--host= prints =host: CADOR=; a test asserts it.
- A clautolisp test asserts the default host is a cador instance (unchanged
  behaviour).
- =--host null= and =--host nihil= produce the same host in clautolisp.
- RELEASE_NOTES entry (the dry-run output changes); version bump.
